---
import BaseLayout from '../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { scenes } from '../../../config/images';
import Breadcrumbs from '../../../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import { aspects } from '../../../data/aspects';
const crumbs = [
  { label: 'Explore Astrology', href: '/explore/' },
  { label: 'Aspects', href: '/explore/aspects/' },
];
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Aspects. Relationships within the chart"
  description="Aspects are meaningful angular relationships between planets. Learn conjunctions, sextiles, squares, trines, and oppositions without reducing them to good or bad."
  path="/explore/aspects/"
  breadcrumbs={crumbs}
>
  <Breadcrumbs crumbs={crumbs} />
  <section class="hero hero--split">
    <div class="container">
      <div>
      <p class="eyebrow">Explore Astrology</p>
      <h1>Aspects</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        Aspects are relationships between chart factors: the angles planets make to one another.
        They show how different functions in the chart meet, reinforce, challenge, interrupt, or
        complicate one another. This is one of the places where astrology stops being a list and
        starts becoming a pattern.
      </p>
      </div>
      <img
        class="hero__img"
        src={scenes.aspects.src}
        srcset={scenes.aspects.srcset}
        sizes="100vw"
        alt={scenes.aspects.alt}
        width={scenes.aspects.width}
        height={scenes.aspects.height}
        fetchpriority="high"
      />
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container prose flow" style="margin-bottom: var(--space-8);">
      <h2>Not simply good or bad</h2>
      <p>
        I am cautious with the old shorthand of "easy" and "hard" aspects. Some aspects tend to
        describe more friction; others more flow. But flow can be underused, friction can become
        productive, and neither tells you by itself how a person will live the configuration. A
        square is not a verdict. A trine is not a guarantee.
      </p>
      <p>
        What matters is which planets are involved, how close the aspect is, what else those planets
        are doing in the chart, and how the pattern is actually showing up in the person's life. The
        geometry gives structure. Interpretation still requires synthesis.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="container grid grid--3">
      {
        aspects.map((a) => (
          <article class="card">
            <span class="glyph" aria-hidden="true">{a.glyph}</span>
            <h2 style="font-size: var(--text-xl); margin: 0;">
              <a href={`/explore/aspects/${a.slug}/`}>{a.name}</a>
            </h2>
            <p class="card__meta">{a.angle}</p>
            <p style="margin: 0;">{a.nature}</p>
          </article>
        ))
      }
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--alt">
    <div class="container prose flow">
      <h2>Where relationships become patterns</h2>
      <p>
        When several planets connect through multiple aspects, larger
        <a href="/explore/chart-patterns/">chart patterns</a> can emerge: T-squares, grand trines,
        stelliums, and other configurations. Aspects are also central to
        <a href="/explore/transits/">timing</a>, because moving planets form new relationships to
        natal chart factors over time. In both cases, the meaning comes from the network, not from
        one line drawn across the wheel.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
